<title>FRANCE: TENNIS-LATEST FRENCH OPEN WOMEN'S SINGLES RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-LATEST FRENCH OPEN WOMEN'S SINGLES RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Women's singles results on the third day of the French Open tennis tournament on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Prefix number denotes seeding.</p>
<p>* denotes new results.</p>
<p>Second round :</p>
<p>*Virginia Ruano-Pascual (Spain) beat Amelie Cocheteux (France) 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Meike Babel (Germany) beat Helena Sukova (Czech Republic) 4-6 6-4 12-10</p>
<p>Ann Grossman (U.S.) beat Larisa Neiland (Latvia)  6-4 6-4</p>
<p>9-Iva Majoli (Croatia) beat Alexandra Fusai (France) 6-2 6-3</p>
<p>Magui Serna (Spain) beat Naoko Kijimuta (Japan) 3-6 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>5-Lindsay Davenport (U.S.) beat Elena Makarova (Russia) 6-1 6-1</p>
<p>2-Steffi Graf (Germany) beat Amelie Mauresmo (France) 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>Ruxandra Dragomir (Romania) beat Yayuk Basuki (Indonesia) 7-5</p>
<p>4-6 8-6</p>
<p>15-Karina Habsudova (Slovakia) beat Elena Likhovtseva (Russia) 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>7-Conchita Martinez (Spain) beat Chanda Rubin (U.S.) 6-3 6-0</p>
<p>Nicole Arendt (U.S.) beat Laura Golarsa (Italy)  6-2 6-2</p>
<p>11-Amanda Coetzer (South Africa) beat Amy Frazier (U.S.) 7-6</p>
<p>(7-5) 6-4</p>
<p>Caroline Dhenin (France) beat Silvija Talaja (Croatia) 6-2 7-5</p>
<p>13-Irina Spirlea (Romania) beat Ines Gorrochategui (Argentina) 6-4 4-6 6-2</p>
<p>Patty Schnyder (Switzerland) beat Katarina Studenikova (Slovakia) 6-0 2-0 retired injured</p>
<p>4-Jana Novotna (Czech Republic) beat Jana Kandarr (Germany) 6-4 6-0</p>
</text>
